From c7894675fcf0970f367af461ae0c116c37956077 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:13:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(wire): join tangent arcs without zero-length connector
 moves

The wire arc path moves each arc onto its lattice centre with its radius
kept. Two neighbour arcs with different centres then end a few
picometres to nanometres apart, and stitch wrote a connector line across
that gap. The post rounded the line to the arc end, so each tangent
joint gave a G1 block with no motion.

Two neighbour arcs whose ends are no more than 2.5 um apart now meet at
the mean of the two ends, if the half gap is under a quarter of each
arc's chord. The margin adds the half gap. The kerf and cover laws read
the recorded arcs (spiral reading), so they still check the exact
drawing. A wider gap keeps a real connector line.

Refs #3937
Fixes #3959

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
